bassoricci","html_url":"https://github.com/luca-bassoricci","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luca-bassoricci/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T09:26:12Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T10:48:42Z","body":"After some digging I have more info to share:\nthe problem is in `com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ser.impl.IndexedListSerializer#L108`\n```\nClass<?> cc = elem.getClass();\nJsonSerializer<Object> serializer = serializers.serializerFor(cc);\n```\nbecause `cc#classLoader` always change between reload (as expected) instead class stored in `serializers` `(com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ser.impl.PropertySerializerMap$Single#_type)` is cached between reload and associated CL is always the original CL so Jackson doesn't recognized custom serializer for `cc` and fallback to generic `BeanSerializer`.\n\nSeems that `io.quarkus.vertx.runtime.jackson.QuarkusJacksonJsonCodec#mapper` is never restored between reloads; some code related to `QuarkusJacksonJsonCodec` can has been found in `io.quarkus.vertx.deployment.VertxJsonProcessor`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/2454196245/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"e